---
/**
 * The entry fold: what the record says, and where the stations are.
 *
 * Lifted out of `pages/index.astro` unchanged when the document became ten
 * routes. It is the one block that is not a chapter — it states the finding and
 * shows the network, and the chapter index below it does the rest.
 */
import StationMap from "./StationMap.astro";
import { cards, stations, stationsWithoutCoordinates, trend } from "../lib/data";
import { href } from "../lib/chapters";
import { n } from "../lib/chart";

const latestYear = Math.max(...cards.map((c) => c.year));
const latest = cards.filter((c) => c.year >= latestYear - 1);
const overWho = latest.filter((c) => c.annual_mean > 5).length;
const overTaiwan = latest.filter((c) => c.annual_mean > 15).length;

const sorted = [...latest].sort((a, b) => b.annual_mean - a.annual_mean);
const dirtiest = sorted[0];
const cleanest = sorted[sorted.length - 1];

const lastValue = trend.all_stations[trend.all_stations.length - 1] as number;
const balancedSince = trend.panel.balanced_since as number;

// The headline decline is quoted from the balanced window, not from the whole
// record: before 2006 the PM2.5 network was five experimental sites, and a
// percentage anchored there would be a statement about those five places.
const balancedStart = trend.years.indexOf(balancedSince);
const declineFrom = trend.all_stations[balancedStart] as number;
const declinePct = ((declineFrom - lastValue) / declineFrom) * 100;
---
<section id="hero" class="page enter">
  <p class="eyebrow" style="--enter:0">1982 – 2025 · 82 個測站 · 341,442,552 筆逐時觀測</p>
  <h1 style="--enter:1">台灣空氣品質的<br />長期重新分析</h1>

  <p class="lede" style="--enter:2">
    {balancedSince} 年以來，全台 PM2.5 年均值從 {n(declineFrom)} 降到
    {n(lastValue)} μg/m³，少了 {n(declinePct, 0)}%。同一份資料也顯示，
    {latestYear} 年有可比較資料的 {latest.length} 個測站中，
    <strong>{overWho} 個</strong>超過世界衛生組織的年均指引值（5 μg/m³），
    {overTaiwan} 個超過台灣自己的標準（15 μg/m³）。
    趨勢與水準是兩個不同的量，這兩項結果並不衝突。
  </p>

  <div class="hero-grid" style="--enter:3">
    <StationMap stations={stations} cards={cards} unplaced={stationsWithoutCoordinates} />

    {/*
      Three figures, not three cards.

      They were three bordered boxes with a big number in each, which is the
      hero-metric template — and worse, they were three IDENTICAL boxes, so the
      chrome repeated three times while saying nothing the numbers were not
      already saying. Boxes around figures also make the figure look like a
      widget rather than a reading.

      Now it is a description list: the number is the term, its identification is
      the description, and a hairline separates the rows. That gives the numbers
      more presence at a smaller size (nothing competes with them), lets the
      station names run at a readable width, and removes three frames from a fold
      that already has a map in it.
    */}
    <div class="hero-stats">
      <dl class="figures">
        <div class="figure">
          <dt style="color:var(--c5-ink)">{n(dirtiest.annual_mean)}</dt>
          <dd>
            {dirtiest.station_name}（{dirtiest.county}）年均最高
            <span class="figure-note">{dirtiest.year} 年 · μg/m³</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="figure">
          <dt style="color:var(--c1-ink)">{n(cleanest.annual_mean)}</dt>
          <dd>
            {cleanest.station_name}（{cleanest.county}）年均最低
            <span class="figure-note">{cleanest.year} 年 · μg/m³</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="figure">
          <dt>{n(dirtiest.annual_mean / cleanest.annual_mean, 1)}×</dt>
          <dd>
            島內最高與最低的倍數
            <span class="figure-note">直線距離不到 300 公里</span>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>

      {/*
        In the column beside the figure rather than below the whole grid.

        The three cards came to 550px against the figure's 653px, so this
        column ended in a 500px hole while the same paragraph, sitting in the
        flow underneath, left another one to its right. Moving it up fills the
        first and removes the second: the headline numbers and what the project
        is now read as one block.
      */}
      <p class="note">
        品管規則與資料管線全部開源，本頁每個數字都可獨立重算。
        <a href={href("methods")}>第八章</a>以一份 2018 年的大學畢業專題作為方法學對照組：
        該研究使用 8 年月平均、N = 7,286；本專案使用 44 年逐時觀測、N = 3.41 億。
        兩者逐項比對，量化每個方法選擇造成的差異。
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
/*
 * A figure and what it is. The number carries the weight; the hairline carries
 * the separation that three borders used to.
 */
.figures {
  margin: 0;
  display: grid;
}

.figure {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  align-items: baseline;
  column-gap: var(--space-3);
  padding: var(--space-3) 0;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
}

.figure:first-child {
  border-top: 0;
  padding-top: 0;
}

.figures dt {
  font-family: var(--font-numeric);
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.6vw, 2.7rem);
  font-weight: 650;
  line-height: 1;
  /* Floor is -0.04em; this is nowhere near it, and digits need less negative
     tracking than letters do anyway. */
  letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  color: var(--text);
}

.figures dd {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--text-muted);
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

.figure-note {
  display: block;
  font-size: var(--text-sm);
  color: var(--text-faint);
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  margin-top: 0.1rem;
}

.qualified {
  color: var(--text-muted);
}
.hero-grid {
  display: grid;
  gap: 2rem;
  margin: 2.5rem 0;
  align-items: start;
}
@media (min-width: 52rem) {
  .hero-grid {
    /* The map was capped at 340px and drew 73 stations into it, which is
       what made it feel packed. With a coastline behind them it also has a
       shape to fill, so it gets a real share of the fold. */
    grid-template-columns: minmax(260px, 22rem) 1fr;
    gap: 3rem;
  }
  /*
   * Explicit placement, because the figure now ships two regions: the map and
   * the prose about it. The map takes the narrow column; its notes drop to a
   * full-width row underneath and pick up the page measure there, instead of
   * wrapping at 20 characters inside a 22rem column.
   */
  /*
   * `:global` on the two the figure owns, and not on `.hero-stats`.
   *
   * Astro scopes a component's styles by stamping its own id on both the
   * selector and its own elements, so a rule written here silently fails to
   * match anything rendered by StationMap — which is what happened: the notes
   * row stayed in column one at 462px and kept the ragged measure this change
   * exists to remove.
   */
  .hero-grid > :global(.map-wrap) {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
  }
  .hero-grid > .hero-stats {
    grid-area: 1 / 2;
  }
  .hero-grid > :global(.map-notes) {
    grid-area: 2 / 1 / auto / -1;
  }
}
/* The `grid` utility and its gap went with the cards; the column now holds a
   figure list and one note, and the note brings its own margin. */
.hero-stats {
  display: grid;
  align-content: start;
  gap: var(--space-4);
}
</style>
